@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "osb.dxp.cloud.subscription"

Feature: OSB DXP Cloud Subscription
	Testing automatic subscriptions to DXP Cloud for customers on OSB accounts with DXP cloud subscriptions.

Setup:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dxpcloud.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DXPCloud                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                                |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | dxpcloud.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | DXPCloud                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                                |
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen DXC Automotive |
	| Code         | ZENDXCA            |
	| Type         | Group              |
	| Industry     | Automotive         |
	| Tier         | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts | 10                 |
	| Address Line | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country      | United States      |
	| State        | California         |
	| City         | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip          | 91765              |
	| Region       | US                 |
	| Language     | English            |
	* I assign a user the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENDXCA"
	* I assign a user the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Watcher" to the project with the code "ZENDXCA"
	* I add an order with the product "Liferay DXP Cloud Subscription Std Production" and support level "Platinum" to the project code "ZENDXCA"

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Zen DXC Automotive" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I remove the web user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" from the web organization "Customer"
	* I remove the web user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" from the web organization "Customer"
	* I remove the web user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" from the web organization "Customer - DXP"
	* I remove the web user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" from the web organization "Customer - DXP"
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENDXCA |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Zen DXC Automotive |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View subscription
	Users on accounts with DXP cloud subscriptions should be subscribed to DXP cloud

	Given the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud

Scenario: View no subscription after offering expiration
	Users on accounts with expired DXP cloud subscriptions should not be subscribed to DXP cloud

	Given I edit a project with the name "Zen DXC Automotive" and code "ZENDXCA" to have a support lifetime of "1 Minute" starting "60" days ago for the product " Liferay DXP Cloud Subscription Std Production"
	And I automatically have all expired projects moved to on hold status
	Then the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud

Scenario: View no subscription after customer removal
	Users that are no longer on a DXP cloud accounts should not be subscribed to DXP cloud

	Given I remove a user the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer from the project with the code "ZENDXCA"
	Then the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud 
	When I remove a user the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer from the project with the code "ZENDXCA"
	Then the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And the user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud

Scenario: Request passport access
	Users on accounts with DXP cloud subscriptions should be able to request passports from the passport page

	Given I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I automatically have all customers assigned to their appropriate organizations
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Liferay University Passport Access page
	Then I should be able to the view the Liferay University Passport Access text for users with full access to the form
	And I request passport access with the following values
	| End User First Name    | DXPCloud                                 |
	| End User Last Name     | Customer1                                |
	| Company Name           | Zen DXC Automotive                       |
	| End User Email Address | dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Liferay University Passport Access page
	Then I should be able to the view the Liferay University Passport Access text for users with full access to the form
	And I request passport access with the following values
	| End User First Name    | DXPCloud                                 |
	| End User Last Name     | Customer2                                |
	| Company Name           | Zen DXC Automotive                       |
	| End User Email Address | dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |

Scenario: View downloads page
	Users on accounts with DXP cloud subscriptions should be able to view the downloads page

	Given I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I automatically have all customers assigned to their appropriate organizations
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.2" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.2 Fix Pack 2" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.2 Fix Pack 1" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.1" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.1 Fix Pack 14" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.1 Fix Pack 13" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.0" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.0 Fix Pack 86" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.0 Fix Pack 85" should be visible
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Downloads page
	And I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.2" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.2 Fix Pack 2" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.2 Fix Pack 1" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.1" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.1 Fix Pack 14" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.1 Fix Pack 13" should be visible
	When I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.0" product and "Fix Packs" file type
	Then the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.0 Fix Pack 86" should be visible
	And the download with the name "Liferay DXP 7.0 Fix Pack 85" should be visible

Scenario: View self provisioning page
	Users on accounts with DXP cloud subscriptions should be able to view the self provisioning page

	Given I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I assign the web user with the email address "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	And I automatically have all customers assigned to their appropriate organizations
	And I log out and log into the support homepage as "dxpcloud.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Self Provisioning page
	Then I should be able to view the following options in the Self Provisioning portlet
	| Project | Zen DXC Automotive |
	| Product | Digital Enterprise |
	| Version | 7.2                |
	| Version | 7.1                |
	| Version | 7.0                |
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "dxpcloud.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Self Provisioning page
	Then I should be able to view the following options in the Self Provisioning portlet
	| Project | Zen DXC Automotive |
	| Product | Digital Enterprise |
	| Version | 7.2                |
	| Version | 7.1                |
	| Version | 7.0                |